 The loader hashes and compiles the exact bound source bytes directly, so it neither reads nor writes donor bytecode caches. Its stdlib relocation test moves a phase tree, loads bound stub dependencies and a native-adapter stub from the new location, and checks that preexisting stale bytecode stays untouched even with bytecode writes globally enabled. No numerical source or real warm-state operation is executed by this test.
 
 For a future host, transfer this packet and its bound source donor subtrees while preserving their relative layout beneath the phase directory. All numerical, fresh-warm and predictive checks above remain pending root review and qualification; this portability repair grants none of them.
+
+## Executed-byte custody successor v3
+
+Sealed v2 is preserved with its reviewer finding: matching a cached module's `__file__` to a currently hashed file did not establish which bytes produced that cached module. V3 sets an executed-SHA256 marker and resolved-path marker only after its loader successfully compiles and executes the exact verified source bytes. A cached module is reused only when both markers match; an unverified same-path module is rejected without replacement. Fresh acquisition also requires the supplied native API to be the identical verified native adapter returned by `load_sources`.
+
+`selector.py`, `PROTOCOL.json` and all prospective constants remain byte-identical to v2. Changes are limited to the loader/acquisition identity checks, their stdlib tests, bindings and this note. `DIFF_V2_V3.patch` records the precise diff. Added tests reject stale same-path cache entries and mismatched executed hashes, verify exact tagged-cache reuse, and reject a different native adapter before warm work. No numerical code is imported or executed by these tests. Numerical and actual-warm qualification remain pending.
